On Tue, 22 Jun 2004 16:25:43 +0000, Congressman Thompson wrote:

> Does being hungry exercise Wisdom for Monks?  Does being satiated abuse
> Wisdom for Monks?

Being "Weak" exercises wisdom; being Hungry is just a means to get there.
When you become weak, keep an eye on your turn counter; you don't want to
get into Fainting, because that will abuse the Wisdom you've nearly
starved yourself to exercise.

Note that when you're Weak you're also abusing Strength, and if you are
Hungry then you're /not/ exercising Constitution. So it's an essential
tradeoff, but one to stop doing once you've hit 18 Wis.

Being Satiated abuses wisdom for monks only, and abuses dexterity for
every character class. (IMHO, I'm surprised it's not a wisdom abuse for
every character; I know I feel foolish after I've stuffed myself. :-)

